      "body": "<!-- markdownlint-disable -->\n\n## Overview\n\nEnroll the nightly Spec Decode AL MTP + Other Acceptance step and its AMD mirror in automatic sharding. The hand split (three parallel jobs, each running a different `pytest` command through `$BUILDKITE_PARALLEL_JOB` guards) becomes one plain `pytest` command, which the pipeline generator shards from recorded per-file timings.\n\n## Claims\n\n- The step and its AMD mirror run one `pytest` command over `acceptance_rates/mtp_other/`, and the generator plans the shards.\n- The step stays under the 20-minute-per-shard target, as on other enrolled steps.\n- New tests in the folder are planned automatically instead of landing in shard 0.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `split_check.py`: no step runs the whole suite in each of its parallel jobs.\n- A scoped build of the PR's first commit recorded timings for the new command; it passed, running the step as one job.\n- `/ci run` on this head checks that the planner now splits the step from those timings (3 jobs for the NVIDIA step, 2 for the AMD mirror).\n- Not yet run for real: the first main nightly with the new command. It records main timings, which replace the bootstrap ones from then on.\n\n## Details\n\n- This is the only step whose parallel jobs run different commands, so main has timed `test_mtp.py` under several labels and the planner can't time the new single command from them. One passing build of this commit records timings under the new label first.\n- Each Gemma4 MTP test is longer than one shard's budget on its own, so the planner gives each its own job, as the hand split did.\n- Timeouts are unchanged: the PR's first commit raised the NVIDIA one only for that bootstrap build, and the second restores it.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [ ] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n\n**BEFORE SUBMITTING, PLEASE READ <https://docs.vllm.ai/en/latest/contributing>** (anything written below this line will be removed by GitHub Actions)\n",
